  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "ThinkSR runs through four stages, and the recurrence returns only to the DQ-CTM thought stage while its parameters are shared across ticks.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense carrier, then the carrier is split into windows without leaving the flow. The compact DQ-CTM process reads and updates those windows through repeated ticks. The recurrence returns to the thought stage itself, and the same parameters are reused at each tick.",
