      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first builds a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows while keeping the tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a dense feature field called F. The window operation then partitions that feature field into X. The equation keeps the field as the carrier, so the compact thought process can read and update dense spatial information.",
